RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
November 10, 2014
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date beginning
at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL
MEMBERS - Mr. Allen (arriving at 6:03 p.m.) , Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Mr. Cook (arriving at 6:03
p.m.), Mr. Luna, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Shanor  and Ms. Williams.  Absent: Mr. Valdez.  Also present:
Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Lois Huff, City Treasurer, and Dan White, City Attorney.  The pledge
of allegiance was recited.
Consent Agenda.  (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to be
routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion. There will be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and support by two
other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be considered in its
normal sequence on the agenda.)  Mr. Brown moved to approve Consent Agenda items, seconded
by Mr. Shanor.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present.
[CA]
Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on October 27, 2014.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Shanor declared a conflict of interest (business interest in voucher payable to First
Judicial District Attorney’s Office) and vacated Council Chambers.  Mr. Luna moved to approve
payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Inquiry was made regarding vouchers
payable to 4 Rivers Equipment (replacement lawnmowers for Parks and Recreation Department);
Art Payroll.Com (temporary labor staffing for a performance at the Civic Center), and Freddy
Cisneros (patio pad work for a HOME program recipient through Community Housing and
Development office).  Information on the department’s lawnmower replacement plan was provided
by Todd Feezer, Assistant Director, Parks and Recreation Department, and Mayor Kaysen explained
services provided by Art Payroll and Mr. Cisneros. [During discussion Mr. Allen and Mr. Cook
joined the meeting.]  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present in
Council Chambers.  Following announcement of the vote, Mr. Shanor returned to Council
Chambers.
Mayor Kaysen opened a public hearing to receive public comment regarding a bar and grill
liquor license application filed with the City Clerk’s Office for JSKB, Inc. d/b/a Pizzeria Venti, 112
East 17th Street, Cheyenne Wyoming.  There being no comments or input and purpose of the hearing
having been met, Mayor Kaysen closed the public hearing and referred the application to Finance
Committee.
Mayor Kaysen opened a public hearing to receive public comment regarding a restaurant
liquor license application filed with the City Clerk’s Office for Loveless Investments LLC d/b/a
Camille’s Gumbo House, 1617 Capitol Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming.  There being no comments
or input and purpose of the hearing having been met, Mayor Kaysen closed the public hearing and
```

