referred the application to Finance Committee.

Mayor Kaysen advised the next item on the agenda (i.e.  Public hearing regarding the sale
of a tract of land owned by the City of Cheyenne, located at 206 West Lincolnway, Cheyenne,
Wyoming, legally described as the East 22 feet of Lot 7, Block 390, Original City, to the Children’s
Museum of Cheyenne, Inc., a Wyoming corporation, for economic development purposes pursuant
to W.S. § 15-1-112(b)(i)(D), and in exchange for consideration as provided by Section 5 of the
Project Development and Administration Agreement entered into between the City and the
Children’s Museum of Cheyenne, Inc., dated October 6, 2014. (City Contract # 6242)) was being
re-scheduled to the November 24, 2014 meeting, beginning at 6:00 p.m., to allow state statute
publication requirements to be met prior to the hearing.  He noted an announcement of the changed
date of the public hearing was included on the current agenda as Item #26 (c).
ORDINANCE - Amending Section 6.04.020, Definitions, of Chapter 6.04, Definitions,
Administration and Enforcement; Creating a new Section 6.08.190, Community Cat Initiative, of
Chapter 6.08, Animal Care and Control Regulations Generally; and Amending Section 6.20.020,
Animal Impoundment, of Chapter 6.20, Impoundment, of Title 6, Animals, of the Code of the City
of Cheyenne, Wyoming.  Reporting for Public Services Committee, Mr. Shanor moved to approve
on third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Luna.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of
the governing body present. (#4044)

ORDINANCE - Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a parcel of land situated in
a portion of the Northeast Quarter of the Southeast Quarter of Section 20, T.14N., R.66W., 6th P.M.,
Cheyenne, Wyoming, to be known as Scenic Development (located west of and adjacent to Converse
Avenue, north of Dell Range Boulevard).  Mr. Shanor moved to approve on second reading,
seconded by Ms. Williams.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body
present.
ORDINANCE - Pursuant to Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendments, Section 5.1.2, Zoning
Districts Established, and Section 5.1.3, Official Zoning Map, of the Unified Development Code,
changing the zoning classification from County A-1 Agricultural and Rural Residential to NR-3
Neighborhood Residential – High Density for a parcel of land situated in a portion of the Northeast
Quarter of the Southeast Quarter of Section 20, T.14N., R.66W., 6th P.M., Cheyenne, Wyoming, to
be known as Scenic Development (located west of and adjacent to Converse Avenue, north of Dell
Range Boulevard).  Mr. Shanor moved to approve on second reading, seconded by Ms. Williams.
Comment was made relative to future consideration by City Council members involving properties
planned for development brought into the City parcel by parcel and not as a “whole” area with regard
to community park requirements.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing
body present.
ORDINANCE - Pursuant to Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendments, Section 5.1.2, Zoning
Districts Established, and Section 5.1.3, Official Zoning Map, of the Cheyenne Unified Development
Code, changing the zoning classification from AG Agricultural to HI Heavy Industrial Lot 1 & Lot
2, Block 1 of Plains Industrial Park, 2 Filing, Cheyenne, Wyoming (located at the southwest corner
nd
of the intersection of Campstool Road and HR Ranch Road) -- referred to Public Services
Committee (sponsor -- Mr. Shanor).
